# Documentation Requirements

## Inline Docs
- Every exported function/class must have a concise docstring:
  - **Python:** Google-style docstring with Args, Returns, Raises
  - **TypeScript/JS:** JSDoc with @param, @returns
- Document the **"Why"**, not the **"How"**
- No obvious comments like `# increment i`

---

## README
- If a new feature or architectural change is made → suggest specific text to add to `README.md`

---

## CHANGELOG.md (Mandatory)

Every non-trivial change must be recorded in `CHANGELOG.md` at project root.

**Format** ([Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) style):

```markdown
## [Unreleased]

### Added
- [2025-02-25] Description of new feature

### Changed
- [2025-02-25] Description of change

### Fixed
- [2025-02-25] Description of fix
```

**Rules:**
- Update CHANGELOG before committing or after code edits
- Each line starts with `[YYYY-MM-DD]` timestamp
- Sections: `Added`, `Changed`, `Deprecated`, `Removed`, `Fixed`, `Security`
- All agents (Registrar, Auditor, Executor) must verify changelog matches code changes
- If code changed without changelog entry → add entry or flag the omission
